  "source": "Docs/Chapters/02_PIONEER_10.md: Legendas finais PT/EN e Texto exato de HUD e cartões. Cartões de data com status 'derived' foram traduzidos da versão PT que o roteiro cita; precisam de revisão da R7.",
  "notes": [
    "As chaves são idênticas às de Pioneer10.pt-BR.json (há teste). 'group' separa narrativa, HUD, instrumento e cartão; 'status': approved = transcrito do roteiro; derived = traduzido ou montado a partir do roteiro, a revisar.",
    "Marcadores {count} recebem o número em tempo de execução. Datas em dia-mês-ano para manter o mesmo formato do PT."
  ],
  "entries": [
    {"key": "PIO.01.01", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Pioneer: a word for those who go first. And the name was no accident."},
    {"key": "PIO.01.02", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "March 1972. No machine of ours had ever travelled beyond Mars. This small probe, no bigger than a car, was about to try."},
    {"key": "PIO.01.03", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Eleven hours after leaving the ground, it swept past the Moon."},
    {"key": "PIO.01.04", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "It spins slowly, like a top, and that steady turning keeps it upright and pointed home towards Earth."},
    {"key": "PIO.01.05", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "But far from the Sun, sunlight is too faint, so Pioneer made its own power with RTG generators."},
    {"key": "PIO.01.06", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Nothing built by human hands had ever travelled so fast."},
    {"key": "PIO.02.01", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Mars fell behind. Ahead lay a place no one had ever crossed: the asteroid belt."},
    {"key": "PIO.02.02", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Nobody knew how many rocks lay in wait. Nobody knew whether anything could pass through at all."},
    {"key": "PIO.02.03", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Some scientists feared that a single collision would end the mission."},
    {"key": "PIO.02.04", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "And then, a surprise: the rocks lay vast distances apart, and the route passed millions of kilometres from the nearest known asteroid."},
    {"key": "PIO.02.05", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Only fine dust brushed against the probe."},
    {"key": "PIO.02.06", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "After seven months, Pioneer emerged on the far side, unharmed. The belt could be crossed."},
    {"key": "PIO.02.07", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "So the days were counted. A week. A month. Then months, slipping by faster and faster."},
    {"key": "PIO.03.01", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Which left the greatest prize of all. By November 1973, Jupiter, largest of the planets, was in sight."},
    {"key": "PIO.03.02", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "A world so vast that eleven Earths could stand side by side across its face."},
    {"key": "PIO.03.03", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Pioneer began taking pictures from 25 million kilometres away."},
    {"key": "PIO.03.04", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Yet a command and its reply could take up to an hour and a half."},
    {"key": "PIO.04.01", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Yet Pioneer had no camera like the one in your phone."},
    {"key": "PIO.04.02", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "With each turn, it saw just one thin line of Jupiter, in only two colours: red and blue."},
    {"key": "PIO.04.03", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Red and blue were measured together, but a single photo came out full of noise."},
    {"key": "PIO.04.04", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Adding photos together, the noise fades and the picture appears."},
    {"key": "PIO.04.05", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Red and blue came from the instrument. The third colour would be worked out on Earth."},
    {"key": "PIO.04.06", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Pioneer never saw green. Computers on Earth worked it out, and Jupiter appeared in colour."},
    {"key": "PIO.04.07", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Real photograph, 1973: Jupiter as Pioneer 10 recorded it."},
    {"key": "PIO.04.08", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "It was the first spacecraft to take close-up pictures of Jupiter."},
    {"key": "PIO.04.09", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "These pictures were sharper than anything a telescope on Earth could offer."},
    {"key": "PIO.09.01", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Closer it came, passing Jupiter's great moons and taking the first close-up pictures of Ganymede, the largest moon in the Solar System."},
    {"key": "PIO.09.02", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "For Jupiter is wrapped in radiation thousands of times stronger than anything near Earth."},
    {"key": "PIO.09.03", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Pioneer absorbed more than a thousand times the dose that would be fatal to a person."},
    {"key": "PIO.09.04", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Closest approach. Pioneer 10 became the first probe ever to visit Jupiter."},
    {"key": "PIO.09.05", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "It passed about 130,000 kilometres above the clouds: three times closer than the Moon is to us."},
    {"key": "PIO.09.06", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Jupiter’s gravity bent its path and gave it the boost to travel beyond the planets."},
    {"key": "PIO.09.07", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "It found Jupiter’s radiation fiercer than expected, which shaped Voyager’s design."},
    {"key": "PIO.09.08", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "It also photographed Callisto and Europa, though only in low resolution."},
    {"key": "PIO.09.09", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Jupiter is itself racing around the Sun, and the probe borrowed a little of that speed, rather like hitching a lift."},
    {"key": "PIO.09.10", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "An image of Io was taken too, but it was lost to the radiation."},
    {"key": "PIO.05.01", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Then Jupiter fell behind. There would be no return journey: Pioneer was bound for the stars."},
    {"key": "PIO.05.02", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "First, hydrogen, the commonest atom in the Universe: our ruler."},
    {"key": "PIO.05.03", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Then a map of blinking stars, called pulsars, to show where the Sun lies."},
    {"key": "PIO.05.04", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "The Solar System follows, with Pioneer leaving the third planet: Earth."},
    {"key": "PIO.05.05", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Beside it, the outline of Pioneer itself, so that our size can be judged."},
    {"key": "PIO.05.06", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "And before it, two figures. One of them is waving hello."},
    {"key": "PIO.05.07", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "A gold-coloured aluminium plaque: a letter for an encounter that may never happen."},
    {"key": "PIO.06.01", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Pioneer had been built to last twenty-one months. It simply carried on."},
    {"key": "PIO.06.02", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "13 June 1983: it crossed the distance of Neptune’s orbit, its instruments still working normally."},
    {"key": "PIO.06.03", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "1989: its power was fading. The instruments now took turns, and the command computer was switched off."},
    {"key": "PIO.06.04", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "In 1998, Voyager 1 overtook it to become the most distant human-made object. Pioneer had shown the way."},
    {"key": "PIO.06.05", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Pioneer had shown the way. Now Earth had to listen from ever farther away."},
    {"key": "PIO.06.06", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "1993: to save power, the camera that had photographed Jupiter was switched off, followed by the radiation detector."},
    {"key": "PIO.07.01", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Its signal was now fainter than a whisper. Could Earth still hear it?"},
    {"key": "PIO.07.02", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "It could. Thirty years on, Pioneer was still answering."},
    {"key": "PIO.07.03", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "27 April 2002: the last data arrived."},
    {"key": "PIO.07.04", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "23 January 2003: a final signal, from twelve billion kilometres away, taking over eleven hours to reach us."},
    {"key": "PIO.07.05", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "7 February 2003: Earth listened once more, and heard nothing."},
    {"key": "PIO.07.06", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Its power had finally run out, and Pioneer 10 fell silent. But it did not stop."},
    {"key": "PIO.08.01", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "It travels on, towards the red star Aldebaran: a journey of some two million years."},
    {"key": "PIO.08.02", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Built to last twenty-one months, it lasted more than thirty years."},
    {"key": "PIO.08.03", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "And the name was no accident. Look at what it did first."},
    {"key": "PIO.08.04", "group": "narrative", "status": "derived", "text": "Pioneer: one who goes first. Every great journey begins with someone willing to go first. Pioneer 10 went first, for all of us."},

